From 0deef06433ad3d8530e0d555c418bce46a985633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Owen Williams <owenoak@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:12:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] netlists P3:  UI Graph -- <ui-graph>, a node / edge graph
 with ports, layered left-to-right layout, pan / zoom / fit, and child graphs
 opened inline, in a modal or by drilling in

- GraphLayout:  a small Sugiyama (cycle breaking, longest-path layers, dummy points on long edges,
  barycentre ordering, pool-adjacent-violators y placement), recursive for nodes open in place;
  the enclosing node's ports are pins on a child graph's sides (an edge end with no `node`)
- UIGraph:  `graph`, `child-view`, `selected`, `boundary`;  `ui-selecting` / `ui-changed`, `ui-node-toggled`;
  lazy children (function / promise);  hooks `nodeLabel`, `nodeClass`, `renderNode`, `edgeLabel`,
  `edgeClass`, `portLabel`, `portClass` for subclasses;  parts and `--ui-graph-*` tokens
- docs/ui-graph.html:  a flat graph, the three child views, a generated 150-node graph

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
